<aside class="space-y-6">
  <div class="panel p-5 rise rise-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-ink-400">What gets captured</div>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2.5 text-[13px] text-ink-200">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-iris-400">✦</span>Exceptions that escape Rack and Sinatra requests, Sidekiq jobs and rake tasks</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-iris-400">✦</span><span>Anything you pass to <span class="font-mono text-[12px]">GoodSorcery.notify</span>, with your context and tags</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-iris-400">✦</span><span>Breadcrumbs: each request's method and path, plus your own <span class="font-mono text-[12px]">add_breadcrumb</span> calls</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-iris-400">✦</span><span>The affected user, once you set <span class="font-mono text-[12px]">GoodSorcery.user</span></span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="panel p-5 rise rise-3">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-ink-400">Scrubbed by default</div>
    <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-300 mt-3">
      Passwords, tokens, API and secret keys, cookies, emails, card-number fields and Authorization headers, at any depth in params,
      headers, session, the query string, job arguments, context, tags and breadcrumb data. Filtering runs <em class="font-display">inside your app</em>,
      so secrets never leave the process; the server scrubs again, card-shaped numbers included.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%= render "projects/setups/self_hosting" %>
</aside>
